# Learn more https://docs.github.com/en/get-started/getting-started-with-git/ignoring-files

# dependencies
node_modules/

# Expo
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
expo-env.d.ts

# Native
.kotlin/
*.orig.*
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision

# Metro
.metro-health-check*

# debug
npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*

# macOS
.DS_Store
*.pem

# local env files
.env
.env*.local
!.env.example

# Firebase native config. Not a secret (the values ship inside every APK anyway), but it is
# per-project and does not belong to the source tree.
#
# The globs matter. `google-services.json` alone matched the exact filename and nothing else,
# so `google-services.json.stale-com.diya.Ddetect.bak` — written beside it when the package
# name changed — was tracked. This repository has one commit and nearly everything in it is
# still uncommitted, so the next `git add .` would have published it. A per-project config
# does not stop being a per-project config because something was appended to its name.
google-services.json
google-services.json.*
GoogleService-Info.plist
GoogleService-Info.plist.*
.firebase/

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo

# generated native folders
/ios
/android
probe-output.txt

# Release signing material.
#
# /android is already ignored, but the keystore is also copied here so that a prebuild —
# which deletes the whole android directory — cannot destroy the only copy of the signing
# key. That backup holds the private key and its password, so it is ignored explicitly
# rather than relying on the rule above.
.keystore-backup/
*.jks
*.keystore
keystore.properties

# Preserved and generated release APKs.
#
# The directory rule alone left a build copied to the repository root (detact-release.apk)
# tracked, so the extension is ignored wherever it lands.
/artifacts/android/
*.apk
# Diagnostics export bundles. Generated on demand from the developer screen and purged
# afterwards; whatever lands here is machine-state dumps, never source.
.diag-export/

# Private server storage and Python runtime artifacts.
#
# `server/.data/` is the path DATA_DIR resolves to by default; the bare `.data/` rule below
# matches at any depth, so pointing DATA_DIR somewhere else cannot publish the database and
# the stored originals by accident.
server/.data/
.data/
server/.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.log

# Developer scratch areas, which are untracked today only because nobody has run `git add -A`.
#
# `server/.scratch/`, `server/.smoke/` and `server/.captmp/` are where probes, debug scripts, smoke
# runs and half-finished investigations accumulate while something is being worked out. Several were
# written in the last hour by different people. None of it is source, and two of the three hold
# things that must never be published: `.smoke/` keeps a real SQLite database with stored originals
# beside it, and `.captmp/` holds uploaded files mid-capture. The repository has essentially one
# commit, so the first `git add -A` anybody runs is the one that would publish them.
#
# Probe output is ignored by shape as well as by name. `probe-output.txt` was already listed here,
# and `server/probe-many.tmp.pdf` then landed beside it with a different name — a rule that matches
# one filename does not survive the next probe somebody writes.
.scratch/
.smoke/
.captmp/
*.tmp
*.tmp.pdf
*.tmp.txt
*.tmp.json
